title: Variables
---
<<declare $bookRead = false>>
<<declare $grunerTrust = 0>>
===

title: object_old_book
---
Player: It’s a weathered notebook. The cover says "Meteorological Log," but the owner's name has been violently scratched out.

-> Open the book
    Player: The last pages aren't weather charts... they're sketches. Webbed hands, claw marks, and the word "FORGIVE" scrawled over and over.
    <<set $bookRead = true>>
-> Leave it on the table
    Player: Not my business. I’m here to record the wind, not read a dead man's diary.
    <<set $bookRead = false>>

Player: I hear heavy boots on the stairs above. Someone is coming down.
<<jump Start>>
===

title: Start
---
Gruner: You’re late. The sun is already touching the water, and that means the time for talk has run out.

<<if $bookRead>>
    -> You must be Gruner. I found a book... it mentions...
        Gruner: (Interrupting) You found the ravings of a man who let the silence break him. If you want to last longer than he did, close the books and open your eyes to your rifle.
    -> What happens when the sun goes down?
        Gruner: Reality happens. The kind they don't teach you in your observer manuals.
<<else>>
    -> I’m the new observer. Where do I put my gear?
        Gruner: Put it where it won’t get in the way. And get ready. In this lighthouse, the job isn't watching clouds—it's keeping the door bolted.
    -> Who are you? 
        Gruner: The man who’s going to keep you alive tonight. That’s all you need to know.
<<endif>>

Gruner: Come. There’s something in the back room you need to see. She won’t bite... as long as I’m standing here.
===

title: meeting_aneris
---
Gruner: Her name is Aneris. One of "them." I found her wounded, and I keep her to understand how they think. Don't turn your back on her. Ever.

-> One of them? She looks... almost human.
    Gruner: That’s what they want you to think. It’s their best weapon. Mercy is the poison of this island.
    <<set $grunerTrust += 1>>
-> Why is she chained up like this?
    Gruner: For the same reason we put locks on doors. To keep the outside world from getting in.
    <<set $grunerTrust -= 1>>

<<if $bookRead>>
    Player: (To himself) The logbook... the previous man wrote that she... she nursed him when he was sick. Who is lying here?
<<endif>>
===